{"version":"1","id":"indepth","handle":"indepth","name":"inDepth.dev","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/a892ee0411d04baab326c9ddec88fab5","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-5.4908,"y":-3.1339,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":300,"newest_post_at":"2120-02-20T12:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"0202-10-02T12:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.001667,"listicle_ratio":0.01,"question_ratio":0.02,"avg_read_time":9.390756,"summary_length_avg":328.916955,"title_length_avg":51.056667,"title_length_var":290.540122,"tag_entropy":2.557927,"tag_diversity":0.163333,"top_tag_share":0.38,"avg_upvotes":0.933333,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.01,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.014235,"zero_engagement_share":0.776667,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":1.361203,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.006667,"recency_skew":0.003344},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-3.7647,-5.5882],"cadence_depth":[5.3382,5.9118],"hype_variety":[-3.3088,-6.0],"title_style":[0.8529,2.9853]},"top_tags":[["angular",174],["javascript",63],["general-programming",44],["webdev",31],["typescript",20],["react",17],["testing",11],["css",10]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["The Micro-Frontend Chaos (and how to solve it)","Angular in Depth","101 Javascript Critical Rendering Path"],"outlier":["Exploring the difference between disabling a form control through reactive forms API and HTML attributes"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"1SnYX9G2y","title":"Implementing reusable and reactive forms in Angular","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1415/implementing-reusable-and-reactive-forms-in-angular-2","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/implementing-reusable-and-reactive-forms-in-angular-1snyx9g2y","summary":"Angular provides two approaches to configure and implement forms, these are reactive forms and template-driven. In this article we will learn about two ways to implement reactive and reusable forms that have the capability to be used as sub-forms and also as standalone forms. We will use the ControlContainer and @ViewChild decorators to achieve this.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3313e5f47faa4dcb41f930efcfdca63d","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2120-02-20T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"BkHo2j5Bp","title":"Add Support for Reduced Motion in Angular Animations","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1436/add-support-for-reduced-motion-in-angular-animations","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/add-support-for-reduced-motion-in-angular-animations-bkho2j5bp","summary":"Angular's animation system is built on CSS functionality, which means you can animate any property that the browser considers animatable. Disabling or reducing animations is an important Accessibility feature. We are going to create a service, which will have an observable of prefers-reduced-motion media query. And then, we can use it in components to disable the animations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ffb29c5a6ac43e853a402b805eac77c7","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2112-03-20T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"EHUz1Hbga","title":"How to use TS decorators to add caching logic to API calls","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1450/how-to-use-ts-decorators-to-add-caching-logic-to-api-calls","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-use-ts-decorators-to-add-caching-logic-to-api-calls-ehuz1hbga","summary":"Caching API calls reduces additional requests to the server-side, improves performance, and reduces data traffic. It's also possible to have more elaborate requirements like cache invalidation via an independent request to an external API service and emitting updated data to all subscribers. In this article I'll go over a couple of possible implementations that we considered.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a4f99f6561cd9ea7cb90bb20fd7b91e4","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2110-03-20T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"hytkLOQHE","title":"NGRX Bad Practices","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1442/ngrx-bad-practices","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ngrx-bad-practices-hytkloqhe","summary":"After working for 6 months using NGRX and understanding all of its benefits, now it is time for me to share some practices and patterns I (and often, the whole community) have recognized as harmful or complicated. In my previous articles I have covered Angular bad practices (twice) and RxJS best practices. Let's start with a list of what not to do in N GRX.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1df8b8b9ae189614cf659c82d3f8feee","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2110-03-20T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"taSvdY7bt","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/777/angular-in-depth-joins-forces-with-angular-love","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-tasvdy7bt","summary":"In-depth exploration of Angular, covering advanced features, performance optimization, and best practices for development.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/868c417ef79cfc270240bdaff12f8a88?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":22,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-12T08:03:13.979Z"},{"id":"SSL2OwhFN","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/301/big-picture-operations","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-ssl2owhfn","summary":"Learn about the features and benefits of Angular, a popular JavaScript framework.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0_ODbtD2--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2008","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-22T15:46:30.541Z"},{"id":"jBIJxJujS","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/300/big-picture-overview","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-jbijxjujs","summary":"A comprehensive guide to Angular, including its main featur